From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:46:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: regulator: ti,tps65132: Add OCS OCP2131

The Orient Chip OCP2131 is a dual +/-4.0..6.0 V display bias supply at
I2C address 0x3e with the TPS65132 register layout for everything the
tps65132 driver uses: VPOS (0x00) and VNEG (0x01) take 4.0 V + n x
0.1 V in bits 4:0 up to 0x14, and register 0x03 holds the two active
discharge bits (D1/D0). It differs in what the driver does not touch:
it has no 0xff EEPROM control register and reports device ID 0x0d in
register 0x04 (OCP2131 datasheet rev 1.0, Aug 2021). Allow it with a
TPS65132 fallback.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/regulator/ti,tps65132.yaml         | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/ti,tps65132.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/ti,tps65132.yaml
index 873d9273..bd8f397e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/ti,tps65132.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/ti,tps65132.yaml
@@ -17,8 +17,11 @@ description: |
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    enum:
-      - ti,tps65132
+    oneOf:
+      - const: ti,tps65132
+      - items:
+          - const: ocs,ocp2131
+          - const: ti,tps65132
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
